2206884	The war for Hiigara has left the galaxy in turmoil. The past fifteen years have seen the birth of new possibilities ... and the festering of old grudges. The once dominant Taiidan Empire has fractured under the strain of civil war. The new Taiidani Republic tries to hold the old territories together. Forces loyal to the old Emperor lurk in the new bandit kingdoms, waiting for their chance to strike back.
2206885	While the Taiidani struggle between past and future, the Kushan people have established themselves on Hiigara. Building new cities. Repairing the damage done by the final battle for their homeworld.
2206886	Even a fragile peace has its politics. The Kiith council has been reestablished, and the future of Hiigara is now debated amongst the gathered Kiith-Sa. Even amongst equals, there are power struggles.
2206887	The Mothership still orbits high above Hiigara. Pressed into the role of shipyard, she now builds new carriers to the specifications of each individual Kiith. The need for new ships and the crews to man them is a desperate one. Military and economic pressure on the new Hiigarans is intense.
2206888	Resources and technology are at the command of the council. Kiith, with little or no political power, have been forced to purchase technology from the Bentusi and other races. Hiigaran ships of exotic design now seek their fortune amongst the stars.
2206889	The war for Homeworld is over now. But the galaxy remains a dangerous place. . .
2206890	Mayday! Mayday! Losing air ... tumbling ...
2206891	We've got 3 unexploded warheads on this Tai cruiser. Suggest ...
2206892	Hang in there, Blade 9. We'll have you locked down in a click.
2206893	Careful! Careful! That reactor is unstable!
2206894	Good work with that Kaalel frigate, workers 5 and 7. I'm sure they'll forget to thank us later!
2206895	You got that right.
2206896	Worker 12. Did you track down those suit beacons we picked up in sector 43?
2206897	Sorry Command. We found the suits, but the poor dogs didn't have a chance to get their helmets on. We tagged 'em for the burial ships.
2206898	Attention Hiigaran Ships! We have thrown back the Imperial attack fleet. Hiigara should be safe once again. Kiith Naabal would like to thank our brothers and sisters from Kiith Manaan, S'jet and Kaalel for their aid in battle. Hiigara is in their debt, as are we.
2206899	This is Kiith Nabaal Carrier VEER-RAK, to any Hiigaran ships in range. Imperialist Taiidani forces are attacking. They are attempting to break through and raid Hiigara. We cannot hold them! Require immediate assistance!
2206900	Fleet Command: Understood Tactical. Attention Carrier VEER-RAK. This is Kiith Somtaaw mining vessel KUUN-LAN. We have arrived in sector 112 and request targeting data.
2206901	Good to have you, KUUN-LAN. We've got a strike fleet needing cover in sector 109. Can you assist?
2206902	Fleet Command: We'll send everything we've got. But be advised we are a mining vessel. It would be best if we do not have to move directly into the main battle.
2206903	A strike wing of Firelance frigates are under attack from Taiidani Bombers at this position.
2206904	Tactical Officer: Without fighter support the frigates will be destroyed and that flank will collapse. Send out a squad of Acolyte fighters ASAP to assist the frigates.
2206905	Attention KUUN-LAN. The first Imperialist attack wiped out our sensor grid. We need you to scout enemy positions with your Recon ships. We are planning a counterattack.
2206906	Tactical Officer: We have picked up a convoy of enemy Resourcers with escorts in this area. They must be re-supplying the Imperialist attack fleet. Engage and destroy them.
2206907	Our forces have taken the upper hand. The Imperials are pulling back. One of their damaged Cruisers is in this area.
2206908	Tactical Officer: Track it down and make sure it never threatens Hiigara again.
2206909	FC: We've been asked by Kiith Manaan to help them find one of their Destroyers. The last word the BUSHAN-RE sent was of a power-plant failure. There are reports of Turanic Raider ships operating in this region, so all pilots should stay on the look out for pirate vessels.
2206910	TO: We have found the BUSHAN-RE. She's badly damaged. We need to send in a Worker to help them with repairs.
2206911	FC: We're picking up a dual signal on the emergency channel. Attention BUSHAN-RE! Did you send out a distress beacon?
2206912	Negative, KUUN-LAN. We've been picking up that signal since we drifted into the region. It must be some kind of derelict.
2206913	TO: Source of anomalous signal located. It may be of some value. Recommend sending a Worker in to investigate and retrieve source of signal.
2206914	TO: Picking up Turanic Raider comm transmissions. They must be after the derelict as well. Engage and destroy.
2206915	FC: Attention BUSHAN-RE. Was wondering if you might be able to help out?
2206916	Sorry KUUN-LAN. We barely have Nav restored to the point that we can hyperspace. Besides, even a mining Kiith should be able to handle a few pirates. Thanks for the help. BUSHAN-RE out.
2206917	TO: The derelict is some sort of message pod, but the technology is like nothing we have ever seen before. We will analyze it further before returning to our mining mission.
2206918	We have arrived at rendezvous coordinates.
2206919	Picking up a signal from the CLEE-SAN, but something is wrong. They're being jammed.
2206920	Thi-. . .-ee-San. We have be-. . .-aider for-. . .-inned down behi-. . .
2206921	The CLEE-SAN is in some kind of danger. Find her immediately.
2206922	The CLEE-SAN is trying to transmit some kind of coded data but the jamming is too strong. We need to send a Mimic in past the mines and establish a direct tight beam link.
2206923	Thank the Maker you got through to us, KUUN-LAN. We've been able to use our advanced scanners to access the mine transponder codes. Now you'll be able to see all of them on your sensor manager.
2206924	We have to free the CLEE-SAN immediately. The Raider guard fleet must be engaged and destroyed as well.
2206925	The CLEE-SAN is out of danger. Recommend we escape into hyperspace before the main Raider fleet can arrive.
2206926	Picking up multiple hyperspace signatures. We have company.
2206927	We arrive to secure one prize and find two instead! Attention Hiigaran vessels! You are hopelessly outmatched. Surrender your vessels and prepare to be boarded.
2206928	He's right! We cannot survive against that kind of concentrated firepower. Get the CLEE-SAN docked. Recommend we engage hyperdrive ASAP and escape.
2206929	Honored Greetings, Somtaaw Kiith-Sa. Did you receive our data regarding the anomalous artifact?
2206930	We have. Our researchers agree the signal and design matches nothing currently used by known Galactic races. Where is the pod now?
2206931	We have brought it aboard now and are securing it in the main Hangar bay. What should we do with it? We're just a mining vessel. We are not equipped to study anything like this.
2206932	We are transmitting design specs so that your manufacturing unit can construct a science module.
2206933	Excuse me Kiith-Sa, but would it not be easier to seek help from another Kiith? We are still within hailing range of the Naabal Command Carrier. Surely they would have the staff to-
2206934	NO! A find like this could lead to alien technology that surpasses anything used by the other Kiith. Somtaaw needs this advantage.
2206935	We have a science vessel, the CLEE-SAN, studying stellar phenomena in the Coruc-tel system. They have been ordered to meet with you at these coordinates and transfer over a research team with analysis equipment. This matter must be kept within Kiith Somtaaw. Is this clear?
2206936	Yes, Kiith-Sa. Very Clear. KUUN-LAN out.
2206937	Repeat. . .This is th-. . .-lee-san. We have been atta-. . .by raider for-. . -and pinned down behind. . .-all of mines. . .-ave code but canno-. . .
2206938	Somtaaw Research Team Log Report, Mk. 1.2. My team is aboard the KUUN-LAN and are preparing for an in-depth analysis of the alien device, which was found derelict in sector 112.
2206939	We have set up our analysis equipment in the Hangar bay and are attempting a full surface scan before opening the device, which appears to be some sort of beacon or transmitter.
2206940	The data transmission is in the form of a short repeating tone, threaded with a strange data stream. Decoding it will take considerable time and processor power.
2206941	In the meantime, we continue with our surface studies. Samples taken from the beacon's hull indicate an age of roughly a million Hiigaran years. Part of the beacon appears to have had some sort of organic layering at some point, but this has not been confirmed. Analysis continues.
2206942	Research module? This is the bridge. We've got power fluctuations in your area and the hangar bay. Are you running any tests?
2206943	Not that I know of, bridge. Let me che-
2206944	What was that? What's going on down there? Fluctuations spreading to lower engine module.
2206945	Uhh don't know ... give me a second. We were examining surface material from the alien probe and ...
2206946	What is going on? Now we've got biohazard warnings going off across the lower decks!!! What have you done?
2206947	Something's loose! It's killing us!! You've got to save the rest of the ship. Jettison the lower decks!
2206948	What? How long until you can evac affected modules?!
2206949	CUT US LOOSE!!!
2206950	Kharak forgive us! Bridge to all stations: Emergency jettison protocols engaged!
2206951	The emergency jettison has left us crippled. We must gather resources quickly and rebuild our Hangar Module.
2206952	All ships cease fire! Our people may still be alive onboard those modules!!! Wait for the CLEE-SAN to investigate.
2206953	We need to know what happened to the lower decks. The CLEE-SAN is going to perform some close range scans, but with all the Raider activity they'll need a large escort force of Acolytes.
2206954	More Acolytes must accompany the CLEE-SAN.
2206955	Whatever happened to the Research Module must have spread to the other ships. We have no choice but to deal with them as hostiles. Get a research team studying the tapes and stay away from the Research Module at all costs!
2206956	Our ships were taken over by some sort of bio-mechanical virus, carried on that beam the Research Module fired. We can run a charge through the hulls of our ships to reduce the rate of infection.
2206957	We have hyperspace signatures! Looks like the Turanic Raiders have tracked us down. And they have an Imperial Heavy Cruiser with them!
2206958	The CLEE-SAN is our property now. Be gone or be destroyed!
2206959	You don't understand. The CLEE-SAN and our module have been subverted by something and it's spreading! Do not approach them. Repeat, do not approach them.
2206960	A transparent ploy, even for a ship full of miners! We thought you Hiigarans were smarter than this. Now depart before we claim you as well!
2206961	The fools have made things much worse. All infected vessels are closing on us. We can't survive an enemy we don't understand. We must escape into hyperspace!
2206962	Hyperspace module charged. Now go!
