2207204	Attention Turanic Base. We come in peace. Repeat, we come in peace. The subversion entity we call the Beast has ravaged both our forces. In order to destroy it, we need access to your starcharts.
2207205	Turanic Base, we say again, we come in peace. We need access to your starcharts in order to stop the creature that is a danger to both our forces. Please respond.
2207206	I don't think this is going to work. Raider turrets are now tracking our ships. Picking up energy spikes! Hyperspace damping field is enveloping us. They're going to attack!!
2207207	The Turanic base is emitting the damper field. Hammer away at them until they surrender or their defenses shut down.
2207208	Close with the pirate base. If they won't co-operate we will have to board here and take prisoners to find the stellar data we need.
2207209	Imperialist fleet has arrived The Raiders must have called for reinforcements.
2207210	I don't believe it!. The Imperials are retreating!
2207211	Attention Hiigaran Fleet. We surrender.
2207212	Then stand down and cease fire.
2207213	Understood. Standing down.
2207214	Prepare to be boarded and to surrender any data and personnel we require.
2207215	Agreed.
2207216	We can send in a security team now to retrieve what we need. Send in a Worker to dock with the pirate base and retrieve what we need..
2207217	Prisoners and data aboard. Returning to the KUUN-LAN.
2207218	We have the Turanic prisoners safely secured. Stellar data being analyzed now. Hyperspace at will.
2207219	Situation Report 13.1- With the Raider nav personnel on board we have been able to project the drift of the alien exploration vessel.
2207220	Location data has been locked in and we will be correcting course. We should have little trouble since the Beast forces we have been fighting could not have this data yet.
2207221	With the raiders aboard I have doubled internal security.
2207222	We have fires across decks J through R! Deck M is venting to space! No word from Engineering! Have we been hit!?
2207223	Negative on weapon strike. Negative! Ship's telemetry indicates internal explosion centered in Engineering.
2207224	Confirm that. Hyperdrive off-line. What happened?! Engineering Module destroyed. Support Module breaking up. Rerouting stabilizer control. Back-up systems coming back on-line.
2207225	Running analysis of blast effect now.... Some sort of massive EM pulse blew plasma lines connecting to drive unit. We brought a saboteur aboard!
2207226	ALERT! ALERT! We've got tracks inbound. Multiple!
2207227	They're enemy signatures ... This is a trap!
2207228	Ambush fleet closing in. We only have access to our capital ships. All smaller vessels are trapped in the hangar deck and our construction facilities are off-line. We must buy the repair crews time. Blunt that attack at any cost.
2207229	Repair teams need more time.
2207230	Incoming capital ships. The Command Ship cannot withstand an assault from those Destroyers.
2207231	Use Ramming Frigates to try to physically push them back from the Command Ship and buy the repair crews more time.
2207232	Picking up a signal being transmitted from inside the KUUN-LAN. The saboteur is beaming our navigation data on the NAGGAROK to the Imperial fleet!
2207233	Saboteur has been found and terminated.
2207234	Assist the FAAL-CORUM with whatever we have, but protect our most damaged ships.
2207235	Launch bays have regained power.
2207236	Construction facilities on-line.
2207237	We've located enemy Carriers at this location. If we take them out they won't be able to reinforce their ships.
2207238	We should look into increasing the speed of our vessels. Engineers are ready to work on an Advanced Fighter Drive first.
2207239	Enemy fleet has been defeated.
2207240	Thanks for the help, FAAL-CORUM! That trap would have butchered us without you.
2207241	Hyperspace module repaired. Prepare to engage. The Imperial Taiidani must still think they can twist the Beast to their own ends. We must reach the NAGGAROK before the Imperials can do anything catastrophic.
2207242	Attention, KUUN-LAN! This is the FAAL-CORUM and we brought friends!
2207243	You have the Gods' own timing, FAAL-CORUM! Could you give us a hand here?
2207244	On our way at maximum burn! We would have been here sooner but you are a hard fleet to find. We barely received your distress call.
2207245	The FAAL-CORUM is transferring command of her support fleet over to us.
2207246	The situation in this quadrant of the Galaxy is grim. The Beast infection is spreading practically unchecked through the reaches of the old Taiidani Empire.
2207247	The Republican fleet is barely holding the line and our brothers and sisters from the other Kiith are spread thin. For every fleet that defeats a Beast incursion, another is never heard from again and adds to threat.
2207248	The Kiith Council is aware of all that you have done out here to halt this infection. The FAAL-CORUM and the ships with us are all that could be spared from the fighting to aid you. They are under your command. The Republican Taiidani are promising some sort of super-weapon to aid in the battle, but until then we desperately need to find a way to stop to this plague.
2207249	Evasive pattern Alpha.
2207250	Roger Command.
2207251	Aye, Command.
2207252	This is Recon Two-One-Four to Command. I have target in visual range. Kiith's blood, it's massive!
2207253	The Imperials are all over it. What are they doing? I don't believe it, they're repairing the drives!
2207254	Understood Recon Two-One-Four. Return to command ship immediately!
2207255	Roger that.
2207256	Come in Taiidan Flagship! What are you doing?! You can't release that ship on the Galaxy!! Do you know what you are about to do?!!
2207257	Yes, they know.
2207258	For a million years we have been trapped in this ship, listening to the electromagnetic chatter of your tiny self/worlds. We know you better than you know yourselves. Your enemies came to use us and instead we shall use each other.
2207259	In return for their help, the ones known as Imperials will be given half the galaxy. An ample return for repairing this ship's systems and leading my children back to me.
2207260	That's madness! What happens when you finish devouring your half of the galaxy?
2207261	Irrelevant. How many thousands of your flickering lifespans will that take? Join us or be destroyed.
2207262	We will stop this!!
2207263	Then be destroyed and join us anyway. Taiidani, honor our bargain and eradicate these Hiigarans.
2207264	Gather our fleet into a defensive formation. We need a sample of the original Beast. Hold off the Imperialist fleet and slip a Mimic in to dock with the NAGGAROK.
2207265	We need an edge in these large fleet battles. Our engineers are ready to design a Dreadnought class battleship.
2207266	The Beast Mothership has hyperspaced into the sector and is on an intercept vector. The Imperials must have called them in.
2207267	Our Mimic has been detected by the Imperial proximity sensors.
2207268	We move again! It is time, my allies, to lead us to this weapon you spoke of. Then we will feed and the carving of empires can begin.
2207269	The Beast and most of the Imperialist ships have gone into hyperspace. We have to fight our way out of this and capture a Taiidan ship. Someone on-board will be able to tell us what weapon the Beast was talking about.
2207270	Situation Report 14.7-Interrogation of the prisoner has revealed a possible destination of the joint Beast/Imperialist fleet.
2207271	The Imperialist had information on a large Republican Naval shipyard at the edge of this sector. They think this shipyard is secretly constructing a new prototype defense station under the codename: Nomad Moon. This must be the super-weapon system the Republicans were promising. There is a high probability the Beast will try and seize this new station and turn it against us.
2207272	After analyzing the sample of Beast material we obtained from the NAGGAROK, we have adapted the main gun for maximum effect on Beast cell structure. In theory it should cause a massive energy feedback in any Beast material. Unfortunately, we have yet to find a way around our own energy overload problems, and are unable to fire the gun more than once.
2207273	Our engineers have found many systems in the gun are derived from basic Bentusi technology. We need to home in on one of their trade ship signals and ask for help with the cannon's power systems. Without this Cannon fully operational, it's only a matter of time before the Beast reaches Hiigara.
2207274	ATTENTION Bentusi fleet, this is Hiigaran Mining Vessel KUUN-LAN. We are in desperate need of your aid. ... Bentusi trade ships! Please come in!
2207275	We will not be bound!
2207276	The energy readings on that hyperspace gate are off the scale. They must be jumping to another galaxy! They're immune to EMP effects, and we don't want to fire on them so the only way to stop them from leaving is to destroy that gate!
2207277	Do not attempt to stop our translocation! Cease your attacks or be destroyed. Do you not understand what has happened? WE WILL NOT BE BOUND!
2207278	Attention all ships! Do not enter the jump gate! It'll tear our ships apart!
2207279	Strike craft launching from the Bentusi trade stations. They're similar to Acolyte class fighters...but their configuration.... it's like nothing we've ever seen before!
2207280	Fleet! Full speed ahead! We have to block the entrance to the gate! We can't let them through.
2207281	Those fighters are armed with ion beam cannons! They'll cut us to pieces, but we can't let the Bentusi desert us. Hold them off and bring down that gate!!
2207282	Use Sentinels to shield our capital ships!
2207283	You are mad! It will take irrecoverable time to repair the slipgate. The Devourer will find us by then! Each of us that is consumed takes the story of a thousand bound worlds with them. The creature will devour all our songs. All knowledge will serve its Hunger.
2207284	Listen to us! We need your help. We are not here to harm you, but if you leave, the Beast will win. You helped us to win our Homeworld. You cannot run away now!
2207285	We aided the S'jet persona who was newly Unbound. You are not S'jet. Your bound bodies and flicker-lives make you blind. And now we will all pay for your blindness.
2207286	Kiith's blood!!! More stations coming out of hyperspace. They're powering up main weapons. We don't have a chance! Prepare to engage hyperspace module!
2207287	Negative! Without that cannon working, we're as good as dead. Better to be blown to atoms now than wait for the Beast to hunt us down.
2207288	You are killing us!! You and your precious stories! Who will remember the crew of that ship? Or are "flicker-lives" not worth remembering?
2207289	You seek to trap us in a diseased Galaxy. This cannot be. Desist and we will allow you to leave. We . . . regret the loss of your memories.
2207290	REGRET?! We regret the loss of the whole sand-cursed Galaxy!!! Stop murdering us and help us kill the Beast!
2207291	They've stopped firing. Keep it up. You're getting through to them.
2207292	The Devourer cannot be stopped. We must flee or even memory will die. We will not be Bound.
2207293	Yes, yes! You will not be bound--whatever that means! Well, guess what: we won't let you go. It doesn't matter how we die. One ancient monster is as good as another.
2207294	We. . .are. . .not. . .monsters.
2207295	Aren't you? Look around. Look what you've done to our fleet. All because we dared to get in your way! Look at yourselves--the Aloof and Mighty Bentusi! Slaughtering the people who asked for your help. You're worse than the Beast. At least the Beast doesn't pretend to be righteous.
2207296	We fear. For the first time in countless orbits. . .We fear.
2207297	Join the Kiith! We're not blind, just scared. As scared as you. Now are you going to help us, or are we going to have to ram this mining ship down the throat of the first station that approaches?
2207298	That will not be necessary. We see our own madness reflected in yours. We will do what we can to help.
2207299	To understand our fear, you must know our nature. We are one with our vessels, as was your S'jet persona. We are Unbound. The solar winds blow across our skin. Hyperspace sings in our ears. The Universe unfolds around our thoughts.
2207300	The Devourer does not kill us when it tries to take our ships. It leaves us in place, but corrupts our being. We die, but we are not dead. We would be trapped, slaves within our own bodies, eternally.
2207301	We have analyzed your weapon and it shows great promise. You are most clever for Bound persons. We are transferring the data you will need to construct reinforced superconductor heat sinks. These should allow you to fire your cannon repeatedly.
2207302	The Devourer has many selves spreading infection through this sector now. You would do well to test your weapon on one of these lesser creatures.
2207303	Attention Kiith Manaan Fleet. This is the Somtaaw mining vessel KUUN-LAN. Please come in.
2207304	Good to see you still alive, KUUN-LAN. Word out here says the situation is grim. It's only a matter of time before the Beast overruns a populated world.
2207305	The Bentusi have helped us devise a weapon that may just shift the sands in our favor. We are on our way to deploy it now. We were wondering though whether you have any data on a former Somtaaw science vessel carrying the CLEE-SAN ID?
2207306	The CLEE-SAN? A frigate class vessel?
2207307	Yes. Have you seen her?
2207308	The thing led the attack on a Scout base. Used her sensor rig to deactivate the sentinel web. We are on our way to track down and destroy the subverted ships before they infect the sector. Transmitting all our telemetry on her position now. Why do you want her in particular?
2207309	The CLEE-SAN was the first ship infected by the Beast Mothership. It should have the most direct communication line to its parent. If we can capture the CLEE-SAN we can lay a trap for the Mothership.
2207310	You Somtaaw have guts, that's all I can say. Good Luck, KUUN-LAN. We will spread the word about what you're trying to do. Manaan Fleet Command out.
2207311	The CLEE-SAN's last reported position is in this area. Send out a flight of Recon fighters to track her down.
2207312	We were not counting on the CLEE-SAN having such a large escort fleet. We have to destroy her escorts while maneuvering in close enough to fire the Cannon on the CLEE-SAN. Remember to only take one shot when the target is in the 50% range band. We need the CLEE-SAN intact.
2207313	The CLEE-SAN is in range. Prepare to fire.
2207314	We've done it! The Cannon works and it is still fully operational! The CLEE-SAN no longer has a Beast energy signature.
2207315	We have destroyed the CLEE-SAN before the fake signal could be sent. We have failed.
2207316	The blast badly damaged the CLEE-SAN. Her reactor core is going critical. Use a Worker to get a boarding team over there right away.
2207317	KUUN-LAN! Come in! You would not believe what the inside of the CLEE-SAN looks like! The surviving bio-circuitry alone could revolutionize our ship tech!
2207318	Try to remember, that "bio-circuitry" was your own Kiith brothers and sisters, not so long ago.
2207319	Yes, of course We have managed to isolate something that resembles the old com array. Preparing to send the pulse burst now.
2207320	Excellent. Transmit and then get aboard the Worker immediately! The CLEE-SAN is going to blow!
2207321	Ready all forces. Harvest whatever resources are in the region. If that signal worked, the Beast fleet will be hyperspacing in at any moment.
2207322	Picking up multiple hyperspace signatures! It's the Beast Mothership. Ready the Siege Cannon. Engage and destroy the Beast fleet. Do not let any escape to give a warning.
2207323	Burn, You Monstrosity!! BURN!
2207324	We did it. We're ready to track down the NAGGAROK and cut the head off this Beast once and for all. Coordinates for Republican shipyard locked in. Maximum power shunted to hyperspace module. Jump when ready.
2207325	Our prisoner was telling the truth. We are picking up distress calls from the Republican naval base. It's under attack from the NAGGAROK and a huge Beast fleet. We will try and get there in time to help, but even if we can't save them, we must engage. This must end now. Whatever the cost.
2207326	<c=ffffff></c>
2207327	I've lost contact with the moon.
2207328	VICTORY to Nomad Control! Come in, Control!
2207329	Thank the Gods! Reinforcements! These things are all over us. We've lost contact with the Nomad Moon! You have to help us!
2207330	Try to hold on, Republican Fleet. This is the Kiith Somtaaw Warship KUUN-LAN. Will try to send help while you regroup. We need you to transmit all the information you have on this Nomad Moon.
2207331	Understood KUUN-LAN. Prepare to rec-
2207332	Sir! Multiple missile impacts. Losing controls of decks 4, 9 and 17!
2207333	KUUN-LAN! They've gotten through. We won't be turned against our own people. The Moon! You have to get past the prox Sensors! ... minimal scanner wid ... -small shi ... won't trigger repulsor field
2207334	So the miners are now warriors? You have come far, little Kiith Somtaaw. You can still join us and be rewarded, as the Imperialists will be. We can make your Kiith supreme upon Hiigara. Is this not what you wanted, when you awakened my children?
2207335	Not this way! We make no bargains with you. Not now, not ever, Monster. We may not be a true warrior kiith, but we were good enough to burn your first two "children" to ashes.
2207336	Our children are not ourselves. We have been and always will be. With this vessel around us fully functional we will never be contained again.
2207337	That defence station is protecting the NAGGAROK. Destroy the Nomad Moon first and then the Beast.
2207338	What in Kharak's name was that?!
2207339	It was some kind of massive energy shockwave. Analyzing sensor readings now. It was a high power repulsor field, and it came from those small emitters below the moon. We have to get something past those proximity sensors and destroy those Emitters fast!
2207340	Our engineers think they might be able to adapt the Nomad Moon's repulsor weapon to our own Dreadnought.
2207341	Imperialist ships on attack vector. They are moving at half speed. Either they want to see if the Beast can destroy us itself, or they are waiting for something.
2207342	Attention Hiigaran Fleet. This is the Imperial Flagship VENGEANCE. You cannot win. Break off this attack. If you do, we will allow you to return to your stolen world and await the end with your mates and children.
2207343	How can you be helping this thing?!
2207344	What choice do we have, Hiigaran? Your mad quest shattered our Imperial Sphere. You took the life of our Immortal Emperor! Whatever we have been driven to now is your fault. You ...
2207345	Sorry Command. I had to cut that comm channel. They are just trying to distract us from this. Picking up multiple hyperspace signatures in this region. Send out a recon flight and see if this is the other half of a pincer movement.
2207346	Check your weapons fire in this crystal field. They are so close together a stray shot could set off a chain reaction. You don't want to be a ship caught in that field if those crystals start going off!
2207347	It's a Beast strike fleet. This is a trap. We can't fight a battle on 3 fronts! We have to find a way to break out to one side or the other before we are surrounded.
2207348	It does not matter how many of our children you destroy. We are legion!
2207349	Excellent work!! Escort vessels hold off that Imperial Fleet while we take care of that damn Nomad Moon!
2207350	The Moon's shockwave weapon has been disabled. Take that station out!
2207351	The defense station is down! We can finish this if we can just pin down the NAGGAROK long enough to target the Seige cannon on it.
2207352	Wait! Picking up a hyperspace signature! It's right on top of us!
2207353	We cannot stay here! Already the Devourer claws at our minds, twists our thoughts. Open your data banks, Kiith Somtaaw, and receive our aid.
2207354	YES!! The Bentusi have given us the design plans for their Ion Fighter! Reconfiguring construction bays now.
2207355	This is Imperial Flagship VENGEANCE to all Imperial ships, break off attack and fall back to rendezvous point.
2207356	Wait. What are you doing, ally? Continue to attack and destroy the Hiigarans!
2207357	You lied to us, creature. First about giving us the Nomad Moon and then about the Bentusi being neutralized. The Taiidani are no one's fools.
2207358	You are what all life is to us. Food!
2207359	What was that!?
2207360	The NAGGAROK is using an inertialess drive. We need to analyze it immediately and try and figure out how to shut it down. Otherwise we will never be able to get close enough to use the seige cannon on it.
2207361	The NAGGAROK is using a kind of sustained hyperspace field to slide through normal space without acceleration or inertia. Our engineers think the field can be overloaded with EMP blasts.
2207362	You endanger the whole. Come to us, our children. You are needed!
2207363	Picking up massive hyperspace wavefront. From all around us!
2207364	INCOMING!! We've got multiple Beast capital ships in strike formation on rapid attack vectors.
2207365	If those attack groups are allowed to converge on us in strength, we will be wiped out. Intercept and destroy them while they are still dispersed.
2207366	The alien ship's inertial field is down! Move in fast and bring the main gun to bear.
2207367	Think again, Kiith Somtaaw. We can reconstitute your friends and lovers. All who have become us can be yours again. We will makes you gods amongst your kind!!
2207368	Enough!! This ends now!! Gunner, sterilize that thing!
2207369	Noooooooooooooooooooo!!!
2207370	The price was heavy. Kiith Somtaaw burned out the heart and mind of the Beast, but the bodies of their loved ones could never be recovered. All that remained of them was a glittering infinity of wire, mysteries and microcircuits.
2207371	For years to come, isolated pockets of the cancer would flare up to threaten the quadrant. But the new technologies born from Somtaaw's bitter campaign soon rendered Hiigaran ships immune to the infection. In time, the last remnants of the monster were crushed. The Beast never rose again.
2207372	The miners of Kiith Somtaaw sacrificed much, and risked all. For their efforts they were brought into the innermost circle of Hiigaran power. Naabal, S'jet, and Sobanii bowed before them. And from that day to this, Soomtaaw's children have been known to one and all as Beastslayers.
2207373	If you're going to break us out, it will have to be soon though. This Raider force is just pinning us until a larger fleet can get here and board us.
